  "purpose": "Compare two prompt variants of a source-excerpt answer style on the same five declared development questions and frozen retrieval contexts. A model chooses global span IDs; the application displays exact attributed source excerpts. This is an original output adaptation around the same taught local RAG and source-lookup flow, with no new library or model.",
  "continuation_gate": "Inspect every selected excerpt and omission, not merely source-copy validity. Require a complete supported cross-publication comparison, relevant answerable outputs and no critical misleading source/context failure before broadening. The unchanged fact, qualification, abstention and whole-answer/export rules apply. Keep failures; no rerolls, final-set use, paid calls or selection.",
  "revision_rationale": "Both free-prose source-span prompts failed citation alignment; the short one also chose invalid ranges. Exact source selection removes unsupported paraphrases and reduces address complexity to one global span ID. Trade-offs are less synthesis, potentially long/fragmentary quotes and remaining selection/omission errors. It cannot make an irrelevant quote a correct answer. No performance gain is assumed."
